<article class="env-definition" id="0ENJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ENJ">Definition <span data-tag="0ENJ">72.6.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian integral algebraic space over $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>prime divisor</em> is an integral closed subspace $Z \subset X$ of codimension $1$, i.e., the generic point of $|Z|$ is a point of codimension $1$ on $X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>Weil divisor</em> is a formal sum $D = \sum n_ Z Z$ where the sum is over prime divisors of $X$ and the collection $\{ |Z| : n_ Z \not= 0\} $ is locally finite in $|X|$ (Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/0BDS" data-tag="0BDS">5.28.4</a>). 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> The group of all Weil divisors on $X$ is denoted $\text{Div}(X)$. </p>
</article>